<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-205 amendment (bead nexus-r7xao, Sam's decision 2026-09-13): the
    tuple space is a metadata store, not a value store. The engine-side
    java checks in TupleRepository (out / ackWithReply) already refuse an
    over-4096-byte body before any write, but this DB-level CHECK is the
    backstop for any writer that reaches nexus.tuples without going
    through TupleRepository: there is none today, and this constraint
    is what keeps that true even if one is added later without noticing
    the engine-side check.

    NOT VALID (unlike catalog-021's immediate-validate case, and matching
    the fk-002/fk-003 NOT VALID precedent's reasoning, though for a
    different underlying cause): nexus.tuples is a live, already-shipped
    table (tuples-001-baseline.xml, deployed since engine-service-v0.1.114)
    that may carry a pre-existing row from before this bead's engine-side
    check landed, on any install that wrote a tuple in that window. NOT
    VALID lets the deploy proceed without a full-table scan under an
    ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock, and without failing on a legacy oversized row;
    every NEW insert and update is checked from the moment this changeset
    applies. No VALIDATE CONSTRAINT follow-up is scheduled here; see the
    bead for that decision.

    octet_length(), not length(): the column is TEXT, and the limit is on
    UTF-8 BYTES (a multibyte character does not cost one "length" unit),
    matching TupleLimits.MAX_BODY_BYTES's own UTF-8 byte-length definition
    on the Java side.

    Same table for a reply write (RDR-206): ackWithReply's reply is
    written through writeOut into this same nexus.tuples table, so this
    one constraint covers both an out() body and a reply body with no
    second changeset needed.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <!-- ── Changeset 1: body-size CHECK, NOT VALID ─────────────────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="tuples-003-1" author="nexus-r7xao">
        <comment>chk_tuples_body_size: nexus.tuples.body capped at 4096 UTF-8 bytes (TupleLimits.MAX_BODY_BYTES) -- the DB-level backstop behind TupleRepository's own engine-side check. NOT VALID: an already-live table may carry a pre-existing legacy row; new writes are checked from this changeset forward.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.tuples
    ADD CONSTRAINT chk_tuples_body_size
    CHECK (octet_length(body) &lt;= 4096) NOT VALID;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
ALTER TABLE nexus.tuples DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS chk_tuples_body_size;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
